# project-gate.yml.template — kit-shipped CI recipe for YOUR project gate
# (kit feature 008; docs/sdlc/gate-command.md, "CI-held certification" + "Wiring the
# project gate in CI").
#
# The `.template` suffix keeps this file inert — GitHub never runs it. To use it:
#
#   1. COPY it to .github/workflows/project-gate.yml. Leave this template untouched:
#      it is surgical-class, so kit updates REPORT upstream changes to it but never
#      rewrite it — refresh it (or first-install it, in an adoption that predates it)
#      by copying from the kit clone by hand (adoption/updating.md, section 3). Your
#      filled copy is project-owned and never managed by update-kit at all.
#   2. Fill the GATE_WORKDIR slot — the directory your gate runs in ('.' for a
#      single-repo project; the app subdirectory for nested topologies) — and the
#      GATE_CHAIN slot with your exact gate chain from docs/sdlc/gate-command.md (e.g.
#      `npm run build && npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test`).
#   3. Secrets (API keys, license tokens) belong in your CI secret store, referenced via
#      `env:` — NEVER pasted into this file, the gate chain, or the evidence you record.
#   4. Push a governed branch: the run page shows the command, the conclusion, and the
#      commit sha — the evidence triplet for CI-held certification (constitution X).
#      Cite the PUSH-event run: a pull_request-event run executes a merge preview, not
#      the phase commit, and certifies nothing.
#
# Trigger notes: `main` on push is the post-merge safety net (a build/test regression on
# the trunk surfaces immediately); a branch with an open PR runs the gate twice per push
# (push + pull_request events) — trim the pull_request trigger if CI minutes matter.
# Multi-gate projects (frontend + backend chains): duplicate the job per gate/workdir.
# Non-Linux toolchains: change `runs-on:`/`shell:` to match (e.g. windows-latest + pwsh).
# Recommended once this has run at least once: require the `project-gate` check on main
# (docs/sdlc/branch-protection.md) — recommended, never mandated by the kit.

name: project-gate

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main
      - '[0-9][0-9][0-9]-*'
      - 'fix/**'
      - 'chore/**'
      - 'docs/**'
  pull_request:
    branches: [main]

permissions:
  contents: read

jobs:
  project-gate:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Run the project gate
        working-directory: '{{GATE_WORKDIR}}'
        shell: bash
        run: |
          {{GATE_CHAIN}}
